You are building a smart toll booth system that calculates toll charges for vehicles based on multiple real-world rules.

Each vehicle is charged depending on:

-Vehicle type -VIP pass -Emergency vehicles -Peak hour pricing -Vehicle number rules

Your task is to compute the bill for each vehicle and print a final summary.

Billing Rules:
Vehicle Type Charges:
Type Vehicle Charge 1 Bike ₹20 2 Car ₹50 3 Truck ₹100 4 Emergency ₹0

Emergency Rule (Highest Priority)
If type = 4 Toll = 0 Skip all other rules

VIP Rule:
If vip = 1 Toll = 0 Skip all other rules

Peak Hour Rule:
If hour is between 17 and 20 (inclusive) Add 20% extra

Number Rule:
Even number → ₹10 discount Odd number → ₹5 extra

Priority Order:
Emergency → VIP → Base Price → Peak → Even/Odd

Input Format

n type[0] type[1] ... type[n-1] number[0] number[1] ... number[n-1] vip[0] vip[1] ... vip[n-1] hour

Constraints

1 ≤ n ≤ 100000 1 ≤ vehicle number ≤ 1000000 0 ≤ hour ≤ 23

Output Format

Vehicle Bill: Vehicle (VIP) Bill: 0 Vehicle (Emergency) Bill: 0 Total Collection: Bikes: Cars: Trucks:

Sample Input 0

4
1 2 3 1
101 102 103 104
0 0 0 0
10
Sample Output 0

Vehicle 101 Bill: 25
Vehicle 102 Bill: 40
Vehicle 103 Bill: 105
Vehicle 104 Bill: 10
Total Collection: 180
Bikes: 2
Cars: 1
Trucks: 1
Sample Input 1

6
4 2 1 3 2 4
999 200 101 300 400 888
0 1 0 0 1 0
17
Sample Output 1

Vehicle 999 (Emergency) Bill: 0
Vehicle 200 (VIP) Bill: 0
Vehicle 101 Bill: 29
Vehicle 300 Bill: 110
Vehicle 400 (VIP) Bill: 0
Vehicle 888 (Emergency) Bill: 0
Total Collection: 139
Bikes: 1
Cars: 0
Trucks: 1


import java.util.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        int n = sc.nextInt();

        int[] type = new int[n];
        int[] number = new int[n];
        int[] vip = new int[n];

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)
            type[i] = sc.nextInt();

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)
            number[i] = sc.nextInt();

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)
            vip[i] = sc.nextInt();

        int hour = sc.nextInt();

        long total = 0;

        int bikes = 0;
        int cars = 0;
        int trucks = 0;

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {

            // Emergency Rule (Highest Priority)
            if(type[i] == 4) {
                System.out.println(
                    "Vehicle " + number[i] +
                    " (Emergency) Bill: 0"
                );
                continue;
            }

            // VIP Rule
            if(vip[i] == 1) {
                System.out.println(
                    "Vehicle " + number[i] +
                    " (VIP) Bill: 0"
                );
                continue;
            }

            int bill = 0;

            // Base Price
            if(type[i] == 1) {
                bill = 20;
                bikes++;
            }
            else if(type[i] == 2) {
                bill = 50;
                cars++;
            }
            else if(type[i] == 3) {
                bill = 100;
                trucks++;
            }

            // Peak Hour
            if(hour >= 17 && hour <= 20) {
                bill += bill * 20 / 100;
            }

            // Number Rule
            if(number[i] % 2 == 0)
                bill -= 10;
            else
                bill += 5;

            total += bill;

            System.out.println(
                "Vehicle " + number[i] +
                " Bill: " + bill
            );
        }

        System.out.println("Total Collection: " + total);
        System.out.println("Bikes: " + bikes);
        System.out.println("Cars: " + cars);
        System.out.println("Trucks: " + trucks);
    }
}